    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0300" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 871.6131/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-02T01:00:00+01:44">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1916, 1 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 3, 1.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. As a result of recent Entente purchase of 80,000 cars gram, since confirmed
                    to be wheat, the Central empires threatened Roumania and there was a danger that
                    the present ministry would be changed and a Germanophile ministry with
                    Marghiloman at head placed in power. To avert this the present ministry
                    conferred with and sold Central powers 100,000 cars of different kinds of grain.
                    Financial arrangements not yet concluded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
